# PostHog analytics. A production build (pnpm build) with both values sends the anonymous daily ping, and the usage
# counts the user allows, to this project. Development and autorun builds never send to PostHog. Reports carry only a
# random one-time identifier, and ask for no location lookup and no person profile; whether PostHog keeps the sender's
# IP address is a setting of the PostHog project (Discard client IP data), which PRIVACY.md describes the same way.
# A variable exported in the shell wins over this file: unset it before building (env -u VITE_POSTHOG_API_KEY ...).
VITE_POSTHOG_API_KEY=
VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com
